**What I did**

I wrote the tests for Slice 1. Three files, nothing else:

- `Tests/IcarusContentTests/ModuleIndexTests.swift` — twelve modules load in id order; every id resolves; `ModuleID` says no to 0, 13, -1; titles match the source headings; `normalise(section) == module.markdown` for all twelve; `split` keeps the text and the `[VERIFY]` markers; `split` throws if the document is not twelve modules; `normalise` drops the preamble, the markers and trailing spaces; loaded bodies keep every source line and the Sources block.
- `Tests/IcarusContentTests/CitationTests.swift` — no citation dropped (35 in the source); Routaboul → `.pmid("10066941")`; McKinlay and the module 4 standard → `.iso("17166:1999")` with no link; WHO → `.url` with that link; Miyamura → the DOI with no marker in it and `needsVerification` true; European Commission and Ledo → `.none`; every DOI links through doi.org; no identifier is invented; marker counts match per module.
- `Tests/IcarusContentTests/DeepLinkTests.swift` — `deepLink(3)` is `icarus://learn/3`; all twelve round-trip; wrong scheme, wrong host, bad number, missing or extra path → nil.

The tests read `docs/LEARN_CONTENT.md` from disk at test time, relative to `#filePath`. No source text is copied into the tests. My copy of the plan had no `### Internals` section, as expected.

