**Two places we may clash at assembly**

1. I assert `module.markdown` **contains** the heading line `## Module N — Title`. The plan calls `markdown` the "body", so the code author might drop the heading. If so, that one assertion needs a ruling.
2. Fields like `authors` and `venue`: I only check they contain the right name (for example "Routaboul"), because the contract does not say if a trailing full stop is kept. Identifiers, years, links and counts are checked exactly.

